From: Zhiyi Zhang <zzhang@codeweavers.com>
Subject: Backport real ALPC port objects and message attribute helpers to Wine 10.20

Source: wine-11.17 dlls/ntdll/alpc.c, dlls/ntdll/unix/alpc.c, include/winternl.h
Port object implementation: ecb4de70ab4776173e92c644144331aed12830a9
Helpers: eb5fe5378fa501d39e2a557b68756b5fb73a08fe, a4cc93099631de3610ce41d7d12622cb32368777,
2396da526d4e789801410af7341f6bd581f7e40e
https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine
Local adaptations: Wine 10.20 allocator name, append server requests, guard malformed
object attributes in server; support waiting on a newly created empty port queue. Connection and message APIs remain honest NOT_IMPLEMENTED
stubs from upstream; this is not a complete ALPC implementation. 64-bit experiment only.
Regenerate tools/make_requests and tools/make_specfiles before building.

